@competence_appear
title: Challenge the panel while appearing and publishing every argument
subtitle: Let the Lewica Justice Ministry contest jurisdiction without leaving the President's case unanswered.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and justice_minister_party = "Lewica"
on-arrival: government_procedural_restraint += 5; tribunal_domestic_recognition += 1; legal_dualism += 1; court_user_trust += 2; president_relation -= 2; news_headline = "The government contests jurisdiction without pretending the case does not exist"

[+ justice_minister +]'s ministry files its objection, appears under protest and publishes the
submission before the hearing. The act of appearing gives the panel no clean
claim that government silence conceded its authority; it also concedes enough
procedure for critics to say the ministry has recognised a court it calls
invalid. Court users at least receive one complete public argument.

- @poland_event_queue: Appear under protest

@competence_ignore
title: Treat the decision as a non-judgment and continue
subtitle: Refuse every legal consequence of K 2/26 and accept two branches acting under incompatible constitutions.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and justice_minister_party = "Lewica"
on-arrival: tribunal_domestic_recognition -= 7; legal_dualism += 8; government_procedural_restraint -= 5; judicial_repair_mandate += 3; president_relation -= 6; news_headline = "Two branches act under incompatible versions of the constitution"

The ministry issues appointments and instructions as though K 2/26 had never
been delivered. The Palace answers as though those acts never occurred. Lewica
pleases lawyers who reject Święczkowski's Tribunal, but judges, clerks and
litigants now have to guess which version of state authority will reach their
case first.

- @poland_event_queue: Sign the appointments anyway

@competence_legislate
title: Return with a general appointments and reasons statute
subtitle: Replace the fight over one office with a rule that binds every future appointment, even at the price of delay.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and justice_minister_party = "Lewica"
on-arrival: government_procedural_restraint += 5; constitutional_restraint += 4; judicial_vacancies += 2; court_backlog += 2; president_relation -= 2; news_headline = "A general law replaces the temptation to win one personnel case"

The Justice Ministry submits a general statute requiring published reasons,
fixed deadlines and the same appointment procedure regardless of who holds the
Palace. Vacancies remain open while Parliament works. That delay angers court
users, yet it denies Lewica the convenient fiction that a personnel victory is
the same thing as a constitutional repair.

- @poland_event_queue: Submit the general statute

@competence_bargain
title: Negotiate a temporary appointments protocol with the Palace
subtitle: Use a viable presidential relationship to clear vacant benches without asking either side to recognise the other's whole legal theory.
choose-if: president_relation >= 35
unavailable-subtitle: The President prefers the ruling to a compromise.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and justice_minister_party = "Lewica"
on-arrival: president_relation += 7; president_judiciary_cooperation += 6; judicial_vacancies -= 3; legal_dualism -= 3; government_procedural_restraint += 2; progressives_dissent += 2; news_headline = "A temporary appointments protocol clears some benches"

The ministry and Palace sign a temporary sequence for nominations, written
reasons and disputed files. Neither side recognises the other's account of K
2/26, but several empty benches can be filled without another institutional
collision. Lewica's constitutionalists call it breathing space; its purists
call it a truce with an unlawful order.

- @poland_event_queue: Sign the temporary protocol

