Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 8;
if (!Q.prosecutor_general_separated) {
    Q.prosecution_independence = Math.max(
        0, (Number(Q.prosecution_independence) || 0) - 8
    );
    Q.government_procedural_restraint -= 6;
}
Q.news_headline =
    "Roman Giertych is sworn in as Minister of Justice";
!}

= June 2026 — Column Hall

The President administers the oath in the Column Hall and the photographers get
the frame they came for: **Roman Giertych** with his hand raised, and behind him
the Council of Ministers of a coalition that contains this party.

Twenty years ago the same man sat in Jarosław Kaczyński's cabinet as deputy
prime minister and minister of education. The circulars have dates on them.
Teachers who were disciplined under his ministry are giving interviews by
lunchtime; two of them are Lewica members. The organisations that ran the
schools campaign against him in 2006 are the organisations that put our
deputies into this Sejm.

[? if prosecutor_general_separated = 1: Our 2025 statute holds. He takes courts,
prisons, legislation and the whole apparatus of the ministry, and he does not
take the prosecution service, because the Prosecutor General is now a separate
fixed-term office that no minister of any party can instruct. It is the single
most useful thing this party has done in this parliament, and today is the day
it is worth what it cost.?]
[? if prosecutor_general_separated = 0: He takes the prosecution service with
the ministry, because we never separated them. Every instruction Ziobro's
office could issue about a named case, this office can now issue, and the man
holding it has spent two and a half years publicly demanding faster charges.?]

He is Minister of Justice. The oath is administered, and it cannot be
un-administered by a statement.

= The arithmetic, before anybody says anything they cannot withdraw

The cabinet parties hold **[+ justice_crisis_cabinet_seats +]** seats. Ours are
**[+ justice_crisis_left_seats +]**. Without us the cabinet has **[+
justice_crisis_without_left +]** against a majority of **[+
justice_crisis_majority +]**[? if justice_crisis_gap > 0: — **[+
justice_crisis_gap +]** short?][? if justice_crisis_gap = 0: — which is a
majority?].

[? if justice_crisis_gap > 0: If we go, this becomes a minority cabinet on the
day it swears in its most divisive minister. It does not fall. Poland has no
automatic election: removing this government needs 231 votes for a named
successor, and dissolving this Sejm needs 307 of 460. What it becomes is a
cabinet that has to buy every majority, and the cheapest seller in the building
is Konfederacja, with **[+ justice_crisis_konf_seats +]**.?]
[? if justice_crisis_gap = 0: If we go, nothing arithmetical happens. The
cabinet keeps its majority and loses its left flank, and we spend the rest of
the term explaining a departure that changed no vote. That is not an argument
against going. It is the price list.?]

Two doors. There is no third one that leaves both the government and this party
where they were on Wednesday.

- @rupture_stay
- @rupture_break

