= The resignations

Every Left minister resigns the same afternoon, before the Chancellery can
brief that a reshuffle was under discussion. The letters are identical and
give one reason.

We surrender the housing budget we were three months from spending, the labour
inspectorate reform in second reading, and the clinical guidance that only
exists because our ministry issued it. All of it now belongs to people who
argued against it, in a cabinet whose justice minister is the man we left over.

[? if government_minority = 1: The cabinet is **[+ justice_crisis_gap +]**
short of 231 by the evening. It has not fallen and will not fall on its own:
removing it requires an absolute majority for a named successor, and this Sejm
cannot dissolve itself without 307 votes. What it has to do now is find a
majority for every single bill.?]
[? if government_minority = 0: The cabinet keeps a majority without us, which
means our departure is a statement and not a lever. Everyone who wanted to say
that will say it by Monday, and they will be arithmetically correct.?]

**[+ ko_leader +]** does not ask us to reconsider. That, more than anything
said this week, tells us what was decided before Thursday.

- @rupture_posture: Decide what our votes are for now

@rupture_posture
title: What the Left's votes are for
subtitle: A minority cabinet has to buy every majority. We decide whether we are the seller.
on-arrival: {!
Q.news_headline =
    "A minority cabinet counts its votes and the Left decides what its own are worth";
!}

= What happens to a minority cabinet depends on us

[? if government_minority = 1: **[+ justice_crisis_gap +]** votes have to come
from somewhere for every bill, every appointment and the 2027 budget. There are
three places they can come from and we control which one is cheapest.?]
[? if government_minority = 0: The cabinet does not need our votes to survive.
It will need them for anything requiring more than a bare majority, and it will
need our voters in 2027, which is a different kind of arithmetic and a slower
one.?]

Konfederacja holds **[+ justice_crisis_konf_seats +]**. [? if
ko_konf_partner_line != "closed": KO's channel to it is already open, which
means the answer to this question may not be ours to give for very long.?]
[? if ko_konf_partner_line = "closed": KO has never opened a channel to it, and
the only reason that has never been tested is that KO never needed to test
it.?]

- @posture_supply
- @posture_snap
- @posture_dare

@posture_supply
title: Confidence and supply, on published written terms
subtitle: Keep the cabinet alive, keep Konfederacja out of it, and be the opposition that props up a government containing Roman Giertych.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_minority_posture = "Confidence and supply";
Q.government_support_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.justice_crisis_without_left) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.justice_crisis_left_seats) || 0);
Q.government_minority = 0;
Q.coalition_status =
    "Minority cabinet on published Left confidence and supply";
Q.early_election_risk = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.early_election_risk) || 0) - 14
);
Q.government_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 8
);
Q.konf_normalisation = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.konf_normalisation) || 0) - 4
);
Q.ko_relation += 6;
Q.psl_relation += 3;
Q.p2050_relation += 3;
Q.institutional_trust += 3;
Q.government_delivery += 2;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 6;
Q.razem_dissent += 10;
Q.progressives_dissent += 7;
Q.coalition_blur += 6;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left supplies a minority cabinet bill by bill and publishes the price of every vote";
!}

We publish the terms rather than negotiate them privately: the enacted
programme is not reopened, the housing and inspectorate bills go through in the
form we wrote them, no bill of ours is traded for a justice-ministry
appointment, and every vote we supply is announced with its price the day
before.

The cabinet survives. Konfederacja stays outside, because a government that can
get 231 from us has no reason to pay Mentzen's asking price, and this is the
whole of the argument for doing it.

It is also a party that resigned over a minister on Tuesday and kept his
government alive on Thursday. Razem says so, publicly, using that sentence.
There is no answer to it except the count of what the published terms actually
save.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the terms

@posture_snap
title: Refuse supply and demand that this Sejm end itself
subtitle: The honest position and the one the constitution makes hardest: dissolution needs 307 votes, and nobody has counted them yet.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_minority_posture = "Demand dissolution";
Q.snap_election_requested = 1;
Q.snap_election_reason =
    "The Left withdrew from the coalition over the Giertych appointment";
Q.snap_election_trigger =
    "Left demand for self-dissolution after the coalition rupture";
Q.early_election_risk = Math.max(
    70, (Number(Q.early_election_risk) || 0) + 22
);
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 12;
Q.government_minority = 1;
Q.coalition_status =
    "Minority cabinet facing a Left dissolution demand";
Q.progressive_credibility += 8;
Q.party_unity += 4;
Q.razem_cooperation += 6;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.3;
Q.ko_relation -= 8;
Q.psl_relation -= 5;
Q.p2050_relation -= 4;
Q.institutional_trust -= 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left refuses supply and moves for the dissolution of the Sejm";
!}

We say the clean thing: a government that swore in this minister has no mandate
for it, the mandate belongs to voters, and we will not supply a single vote
until they have been asked.

The constitution answers immediately. Self-dissolution takes **307 of 460**,
which is more than every party currently prepared to vote for one; the only
other route runs through a budget the government has not yet failed to pass. We
have not brought an election closer this week. We have made every party in the
building state, on the record, whether it wants one — and the ones that say no
now have to explain what they are protecting.

- @poland_event_queue: Move the dissolution resolution

@posture_dare
title: Tell them to find 231 wherever they like
subtitle: Refuse to be the cabinet's floor and let it walk to the only other seller in the building. Everything after this is KO's choice and our responsibility.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_minority_posture = "No floor";
Q.government_minority = 1;
Q.coalition_status = "Minority cabinet with no reliable majority";
Q.konf_normalisation = (Number(Q.konf_normalisation) || 0) + 10;
Q.early_election_risk += 12;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 16;
// A cabinet that is short and has been refused a floor by the Left goes to the
// only bloc that can supply the difference. Opening the channel is KO's act;
// refusing to be the alternative is ours.
if (Q.justice_crisis_gap > 0 &&
    Q.ko_konf_partner_line == "closed" &&
    (Number(Q.justice_crisis_without_left) || 0) +
        (Number(Q.justice_crisis_konf_seats) || 0) >=
        (Number(Q.justice_crisis_majority) || 231)) {
    Q.ko_konf_partner_line = "talks";
    Q.ko_konf_line_opened_by_rupture = 1;
}
Q.party_unity += 5;
Q.progressive_credibility += 10;
Q.razem_cooperation += 8;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.2;
Q.ko_relation -= 12;
Q.far_right_agenda += 4;
Q.institutional_trust -= 4;
Q.news_headline = Q.ko_konf_line_opened_by_rupture
    ? "KO opens talks with Konfederacja after the Left refuses to be its floor"
    : "The Left refuses to be a minority cabinet's floor";
!}

We refuse the role of the opposition that governs without offices. No standing
arrangement, no advance guarantees, no bill-by-bill price list. They wanted a
cabinet without us; they can have one, and they can find its majority.

[? if ko_konf_line_opened_by_rupture = 1: They find it where everyone knew it
was. Within a fortnight KO's negotiators are meeting Konfederacja about the
autumn calendar, and the meetings are described as technical, which is what such
meetings are always described as. **[+ justice_crisis_without_left +]** plus
**[+ justice_crisis_konf_seats +]** clears 231, and the door that has been shut
since 2019 is now merely ajar.?]
[? if ko_konf_line_opened_by_rupture = 0: They do not find it. The arithmetic
does not close even with Konfederacja, or the door to it is not one KO can open
this month, so the cabinet governs by improvisation and the autumn budget
becomes the date everything is aimed at.?]

We are clean, we are consistent, and we have made ourselves irrelevant to what
happens between now and the budget. Whether that was the right price depends
entirely on what walks through the door we refused to hold shut.

- @poland_event_queue: Refuse the arrangement

